<testgrp id="RM000000FTZ01FX_04_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___000045E00001">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>TaSCAN (A/T / CVT Learned Value Initialization, G Sensor 0-point Learning and CVT Hydraulic Pressure Learning)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Initializing the learned values clears both the G sensor 0-point learning values and the CVT hydraulic pressure learning values, so when replacing the parts in the table below, perform AT/CVT learned value initialization and be sure to perform both G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="1">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="4.13in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry align="center">
<ptxt>Replacement Parts</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Continuously Variable Transaxle</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Oil Pressure Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw Rate Sensor</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After performing AT/CVT learned value initialization, be sure to perform G sensor 0-point learning first, and then CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Be sure to place the vehicle on a level surface and perform 0 point learning.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not subject the vehicle to vibration while 0 point learning is in progress.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), perform A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0 point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedures for A/T/CVT learned value initialization, G sensor 0-point learning and CVT hydraulic pressure learning, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000021F400AX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs again. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000FTZ01FX_04_0011" fin="true">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
